{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Which HaShem commanded by the hand of Moshe.</b> The Ramban wrote: it does not say 'as HaShem commanded Moshe,' as it says everywhere, because his sons did not do as HaShem commanded, but they did all the things that HaShem commanded by the hand of Moshe, and moreover they added to the commandment what the verse says (Leviticus 10:1): ״אש זרה אשר לא צוה אותם״ — strange fire which He had not commanded them. End quote. And this section of the consecration (מלואים) was spoken seven days before the erection of the Tabernacle, for Moshe on the twenty-third of Adar was commanded concerning the erection of the Tabernacle and erected it, and at the end of seven days the Holy One, blessed be He, Who sits upon the cherubim, called him and commanded him concerning the offerings — all the sections that begin from the portion of ויקרא until here." "<b>And behold,</b> the Tabernacle was consecrated with an offering of consecration (מלואים), and according to what I wrote above on the verse ״כי שבעת ימים ימלא את ידכם״ — 'for seven days He shall fill your hand' — it was fitting that it be consecrated with it, for the offering of consecration is an offering that comprises sin-offering, burnt-offering, and peace-offerings, and so their matter encompasses the entire structure. Therefore Moshe served all seven days and dressed Aharon seven times, from the first, which is the linen tunic (כתונת בד), to the seventh, which is the frontlet (הציץ), in order to draw down the Shekhinah, which is comprised of seven, and then it rested the next day, on the eighth day, which was the first of Nisan." "<b>And the reason</b> for the consecration offering (מלואים), that it should be a sin-offering, burnt-offering, and peace-offerings, according to its plain sense, is that he brought a sin-offering to make atonement for the altar, in the manner of what is written (verse 15): ״ויקדשהו לכפר עליו״ — 'and he sanctified it, to make atonement upon it'; and the burnt-offering to find favor for the priests; and the peace-offerings to give thanks to HaShem, for He did good with them in commanding them to make for Him a Tabernacle and a house of splendor. And so in the Temple to come they will offer a consecration offering with the dedication of the altar, and just as the princes offered at the Tabernacle the dedication of the altar and offered on the Sabbath, so too in the time to come the prince will offer its dedication on the Sabbath, as is explicit in Ezekiel. May the Place grant us merit to see its building and to offer there offerings upon the altar that will be for favor, and may He fulfill for us in mercy the promise of Isaiah, of blessed memory, who said (Isaiah 60:7): ״כל צאן קדר יקבצו לך אילי נביות ישרתונך יעלו על רצון מזבחי ובית תפארתי אפאר״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:14.253484804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}